FC0"}, {"file_name": "2-heart-close.png", "id": "1133964476169705", "uri": "https://scontent-dfw5-3.oculuscdn.com/v/t64.5771-25/491825546_1133964489503037_5171123759215771754_n.png?_nc_cat=104&_nc_map=urlgen_bucketless&ccb=1-7&_nc_sid=6e7a0a&_nc_ohc=O57B20pgBuEQ7kNvwG9pqWA&_nc_oc=Adr8s3ygzUy2KUVS3waWyobRVeFZhhiFsGd-T8etT92My5F5uTeT2RgcIIdfIbAqSzs&_nc_zt=3&_nc_ht=scontent-dfw5-3.oculuscdn.com&_nc_ss=7f20f&oh=00_AQR76jXVDS_S2DWzwLar2AVB5-6ls-rkkbBAAlf3kb0DOQ&oe=6B08528C"}, {"file_name": "1-heartbeat-lungs.png", "id": "1079259535160302", "uri": "https://scontent-dfw6-2.oculuscdn.com/v/t64.5771-25/491823757_1079259541826968_5952060383222830183_n.png?_nc_cat=104&_nc_map=urlgen_bucketless&ccb=1-7&_nc_sid=6e7a0a&_nc_ohc=44yLAugmuSkQ7kNvwEgYDa9&_nc_oc=AdrSEYY_Fa41ZXSi4sC5iefPygrOs5gLY-wPkZHyR-F8d8xluMXgC_FKdzhqieA7e2E&_nc_zt=3&_nc_ht=scontent-dfw6-2.oculuscdn.com&_nc_ss=7f20f&oh=00_AQTZjP484PwGmPowSpMkRscQe2kLi0QnpPXjRW9cVVBxdw&oe=6B085D5A"}], "video_trailer": null, "video_trailer_thumbnail": {"file_name": "trailer-cover-2560x1440.png", "id": "3611590895670981", "uri": "https://scontent-dfw5-3.oculuscdn.com/v/t64.5771-25/491824322_3611590899004314_3689080381546488398_n.png?_nc_cat=101&_nc_map=urlgen_bucketless&ccb=1-7&_nc_sid=6e7a0a&_nc_ohc=q33p1e3LsOMQ7kNvwHJQpYM&_nc_oc=AdoQfI14XLvHU34FbJna15qjf5v2kDy2Diq_tz36Kz9SEtz6B2sANsxTRmBHbrwnpEU&_nc_zt=3&_nc_ht=scontent-dfw5-3.oculuscdn.com&_nc_ss=7f20f&oh=00_AQRy9oD9ECZEBTgJSL9UjLj_5AqOzTSLmEbPg_OgUNhgHw&oe=6B08412E"}, "display_name": "Anatomy Cube", "keywords": ["anatomy", "xr", "human", "atlas", "male"], "long_description": "Anatomy Cube puts a life-size human body in your room, in mixed reality, or in a gallery, under a night sky or at dusk.\n\nThe body is a light glass skeleton. Carry a lens through it: a box, sphere, octahedron, dodecahedron or slice shows the full-detail anatomy inside, from about 3,500 named structures. Choose the tissues, drawing styles and colours.\n\nHOW IT WORKS: narrated sequences on the real anatomy - the senses, the heartbeat, breathing, the blood's round trip, reflexes, swallowing, moving the arm and what a stroke does.\n\nSENSORS: how each signal is made, from the body to the screen, then live: ECG leads, EEG rhythms, a pulse oximeter on the fingertip, a thermal camera reading breath at the nostrils, and an ultrasound probe you move over the skin that builds a 3D picture.\n\nIMPLANTS: placed on the atlas's own bones, vessels and nerves, part by part, with their history, materials and the non-metal alternatives - hip, knee and spine implants, bone healing, an artificial disc, a dental implant, pacemaker, heart pump, coronary stent, cataract lens, deep brain stimulation, a brain-computer interface and an NFC chip.\n\nLimits: the lens is small - about 7-9 cm with every tissue on at the chest or hand, 4 cm in the head, larger with fewer tissues. Signals and devices are simulated for teaching. Adult male model; the inner and middle ear are not included.\n\nEducational use only: not a medical device, not for diagnosis or treatment, not medical advice.\n", "short_description": "Walk around a life-size human body in your room and look inside it through a lens you carry: bone, muscle, vessels, nerves and organs in full detail. Narrated sequences show how the body works, how medical sensors read it - ECG, EEG, pulse oximetry, a thermal breathing camera, ultrasound - and how implants are placed and work, from hip and knee replacements to pacemakers, heart pumps and brain implants.\n"}]}, "developer_name": null, "developer_privacy_policy_url": "https://nebulytic.com/apps/anatomy-cube/privacy", "developer_terms_of_service_url": "https://nebulytic.com/apps/anatomy-cube/terms", "publisher_name": "Nebulytic", "support_website_url": "https://nebulytic.com/apps/anatomy-cube/support", "website_url": "https://nebulytic.com/apps/anatomy-cube/", "category": null, "comfort_rating": "COMFORTABLE_FOR_MOST", "comfort_tags": [], "context_category": {"id": "362692211442873", "context_ca